Third-party components

This product bundles or distributes software from third parties, each under its
own license. They are not covered by the notice above. At minimum:

  Python runtime dependencies (see pyproject.toml and uv.lock), including but
  not limited to FastAPI, Starlette, SQLModel, SQLAlchemy, Alembic, Pydantic,
  Uvicorn, APScheduler, httpx, prometheus-client, argon2-cffi, PyJWT,
  cryptography, transformers and huggingface-hub.

  gpustack-runtime — the containerized inference deployer, imported by every
  inference backend. Distributed as a separate package under its own license.

  gpustack-higress-plugins — the gateway wasm plugins and their router,
  distributed as a separate package under its own license.

  Higress / Envoy components, packaged into the container image as
  mirrored-higress-{api-server,higress,pilot,gateway}.

  PostgreSQL, bundled in the container image.

  Helm chart subcharts and the operator image referenced by
  charts/gpustack-chart and pack/Dockerfile.

  Vendor and model icons under static/catalog_icons/ and docs/assets/logos/,
  which are the trademarks and copyrighted works of their respective owners
  (including AMD, Huawei/Ascend, Cambricon, Hygon, Iluvatar, MetaX, Moore
  Threads, NVIDIA, T-Head and various model publishers). They are reproduced
  solely to identify compatible hardware and model families, unmodified, and no
  affiliation or endorsement is implied.

  The web console (a separate repository) bundles further third-party
  components, including UmiJS, React, Ant Design, Monaco Editor and ECharts;
  see that repository's own lockfile and notices.

For an authoritative, machine-generated inventory of the components actually
shipped in a given build, generate an SBOM and a license report rather than
relying on this list:

    syft <image-or-artifact> -o spdx-json > sbom.json
